      "id": "sha256:193c2b3f9a0d241da44b1ebe0d76a1e2fa962632c99e57ff396326055471f096",
      "title": "Show HN: Corgi, a helpful {agent, terminal} multiplexer",
      "url": "https://corgi.computer/",
      "source_feed_ids": [
        "hacker-news-frontpage"
      ],
      "published_at": "2026-10-23T19:46:38Z",
      "authors": [
        "eiopa"
      ],
      "categories": [],
      "guid": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50214373",
      "summary": "Hey everyone, Inspired by Herdr, I've built an agent multiplexer that I've been using as my daily driver for a few weeks now. I think I improved on the concept in a few ways, focusing on the ergonomics I always wished I had: I show you what the agents are up to, along with a running feed of their activity. There's also a simple shortcut (F1) to go to the next unread agent. I use multiple accounts, so I've added unified launcher for Codex/Claude Code/Pi. Theres some careful ergonomics there: fast search and resume over sessions, inline usage tracking etc. Many small quality of life improvements to the terminal experience: - Links can be copied with a click, so no need to drag-select over many lines - cmd+v just pastes images (even on SSH) - images have a thumbnail preview. - Built-in CPU/Memory/GPU usage tracking, broken down by workspace I assume you have access to cheap inference (Luna/Haiku/etc). It just reuses the agents to organize things for you: what is this http link? what is this worktree about? what is each agent doing? It's small but it made my environment feel more cozy. On a personal note, I've been on a frustrating sick leave for a while now. I created Corgi to challenge myself, and see if I can go back. The answer is more mixed than I had hoped, but I am happy with the result and thankful for the experience. I hope you like it! a few friends & myself have been using it for a few weeks and it's been pretty nice. There's still a lot to improve and some rough edges, so feedback would be greatly appreciated. Thank you :) Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50214373 Points: 34 # Comments: 4",
      "published_raw": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:46:38 +0000",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-23T19:46:38Z",
      "updated_raw": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:46:38 +0000",
      "language": "en"
    },
